  "image_tag": "bench-glom",
  "instruction": "## Goal\n\nExtend glom so that arguments passed to several core and matching constructs can themselves be evaluated as specs against the current target. This affects `Coalesce` defaults, `Call` arguments, `Match`/`Switch`/`Check` matching, `Assign` values, and `T`-expression subspecs. The change should make nested spec evaluation work recursively and consistently across `glom.core`, `glom.matching`, and `glom.mutation`.\n\n## Observable behavior\n\n```python\n# From test_spec_and_recursion\ndef test_spec_and_recursion():\n    assert repr(Spec('a.b.c')) == \"Spec('a.b.c')\"\n\n    # Call doesn't normally recurse, but Spec can make it do so\n    assert glom(\n        ['a', 'b', 'c'],\n        Call(list, args=(\n            Spec(Call(reversed, args=(Spec(T),))),)\n        )) == ['c', 'b', 'a']\n    assert glom(['cat', {'cat': 1}], T[1][T[0]]) == 1\n    assert glom(\n        [['ab', 'cd', 'ef'], ''.join],\n        Call(T[1], args=(Auto((T[0], [T[1:]])),))) == 'bdf'\n\n    # test that spec works on the left of a dict spec\n    assert glom({'a': 'A'}, {Spec('a'): 'a', 'a': 'a'}) == {'A': 'A', 'a': 'A'}\n```\n\n```python\n# From test_match_default\ndef test_match_default():\n    # test that default works with Match\n    assert glom({'a': 'b'}, Match({'a': 'b'}, default='c')) == {'a': 'b'}\n    assert glom({'a': 'b'}, Match({'a': 'x'}, default='c')) == 'c'\n    assert glom({'a': 'b'}, Match({'a': 'x'}, default=Spec('a'))) == 'b'\n```\n\n## Constraints\n\n- Keep the public API of `glom.core.glom`, `glom.core.Coalesce`, `glom.core.Call`, `glom.matching.Match`, `glom.matching.Switch`, `glom.matching.Check`, and `glom.mutation.Assign` unchanged.\n- Files in scope: `glom/__init__.py`, `glom/core.py`, `glom/grouping.py`, `glom/matching.py`, `glom/mutation.py`, `glom/reduction.py`, `glom/reprlib_backport.py`, `glom/streaming.py`, and the test files under `glom/test/`.\n\n## How success is measured\n\n```\npython -m pytest -q glom/test/test_basic.py::test_spec_and_recursion glom/test/test_match.py::test_match_default glom/test/test_match.py::test_switch glom/test/test_mutation.py::test_assign_spec_val glom/test/test_path_and_t.py::test_t_subspec glom/test/test_scope_vars.py::test_s_scope_assign\n```",
